# 
# IN-SCOPE. Section 2 commissions exactly this measurement — "does the
# single-photo export of a frame differ from its preview" — and forbids acting
# ahead of it: "Do not fix anything until the measurement says which it is." The
# measurement came first and landed on the plan's own second branch, "the new arm
# has a defect in how it drives the export and the app is fine". The fix followed
# it, with the number on the named frame NIR_1651 and both reads stated, which is
# the plan's Verification requirement discharged.
# 
# The breadth of the walk change is COMPELLED rather than chosen: the defect was
# in `dHue`, shared by arm 2, the tile arm and arm 4, so replacing it forces all
# three bars into new units. The file header and arm 4's comment both documented
# the statistic being removed and asserted the claim the measurement refuted;
# leaving either would commit a source comment asserting a falsehood about the
# function below it, in a repository whose architecture document is generated from
# file-opening comments.
# 
# The judge declined the earlier reading that the Files sentence "prescribes
# nothing". Read strictly, "the assertion belongs in tools/agreement-walk.mjs as a
# fifth arm" authorises no committed instrument at all. What carries the commit
# past it is that the plan's own diagnosis frame contemplates the ARM being at
# fault, so the repair is to the thing the plan put in doubt rather than to a new
# subject.
# 
# FIVE ITEMS THE PLAN DOES NOT COVER, allowed on repository standing practice and
# named rather than absorbed:
# 
# - IR-SCIENCE.md section 6's standing-error passage. No plan text mentions the
#   file. Its authority is that IR-SCIENCE.md is where standing errors live, each
#   with the measurement that established it, and the removed header cited section
#   6's metric by name, so that is the refuted claim's home. This is the thinnest
#   authority in the commit.
# - The NOTES tile paragraph. The strip tile path is a subject the plan never
#   touches; it is reached only through TILE_BAR, which is itself collateral. It
#   was allowed because TILE_BAR could not be set honestly from a number alone —
#   a residual that moves is not a defect that shows — and because the paragraph
#   is deliberately terminal: not diagnosed, not ranked, no bullet, no record.
#   One more sentence in that direction would have tipped it.
# - TILE_BAR = 20 as a tolerance sized around a five-degree residual the diff
#   itself calls NOT established. The plan authorises no tolerance-setting on the
#   tile path; the arm cannot keep a 30-degree threshold once the units change.
# - The 030 roadmap bullet's implementation write-up. The plan's "Not in this
#   plan" fences off finishing 030's aimed arm. Only the verification sentence
#   traces to the plan; a bullet cannot say "verified on export" without naming
#   what was verified.
# - The 051 archive move, its Outcome, and the `fix.pts` Float32Array defect
#   reported inside it. Bookkeeping for section 1's promotion and for work already
#   on the branch, not named in the plan. The claimed source fix was checked and
#   is in f7f4226, already an ancestor of origin/main.
# 
# AND ONE DEFECT THE JUDGE FOUND IN THE COMMIT AS FIRST STAGED, not about scope:
# `.plan-scope` carried commit A's verdict — "Content diff is empty" — while
# sitting inside this 592-line commit touching four content files. A record about
# a different commit than the one claiming it is the failure this repository's
# decision gate refuses elsewhere. This recording replaces it.
# 
# ADDENDUM, ADDED AFTER THE JUDGEMENT ABOVE AND SELF-JUDGED, said plainly rather
# than folded into the subagent's verdict.
# 
# `docs/decisions/030-a-mask-can-only-act-in-one-place.md` gains a
# "## Built already" section. It was not in the diff the judge read.
# 
# It is COMPELLED BY A GATE rather than chosen. Archiving 051 — which the judge
# allowed as the promotion's bookkeeping — put 030 at rank 1, and
# `tools/decisions-check.mjs` refuses a commit when the next-up record has no
# "## Built already": list what EXISTS before starting an item, or a second one
